=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  config edit-syslog -------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Proposed: no Figma frame. syslogServers: three servers. Add$
# asks the address, the protocol, the port and, for tls, the CA$
# file; the same address and port again is refused by the whole$
# list's check.$
$
# Edit a setting ###############################################$
$
   1) username             george$
   2) sshKeys              1 key$
   3) sshPort              2222$
   4) disableRootSSH       true$
   5) enableUfwSshPolicy   true$
   6) configureDns         true$
   7) syslogServers        logs.example.net, 192.0.2.51, 192....$
   8) ntpServers           None$
   9) kernel               false$
  10) confirmTimeout       3m$
  11) checkReleases        false$
  12) enableAutoUpdates    true$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-12 or q]: $
$
# syslogServers ################################################$
$
  Servers ------------------------------------------------------$
$
   -  Server               logs.example.net:6514 TLS$
   -  Server               192.0.2.51:514 TCP$
   -  Server               192.0.2.52:514 UDP$
$
   1) Add server$
   2) Remove server$
   3) Change protocol$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: $
$
# syslogServers ################################################$
$
   1. Enter syslog server [0 or q]: $
$
   2. Enter protocol [tcp] [0 or q]: $
$
   3. Enter port [514] [0 or q]: $
  (x) The same address and port as server 2$
   3. Enter port [514] [0 or q]: $
$
   -  Save the configuration$
      /etc/hardn/hardn.yml$
      @@ -21,3 +21,6 @@$
         - server: "192.0.2.51"$
         - server: "192.0.2.52"$
           protocol: udp$
      +  - server: 192.0.2.51$
      +    port: 1514$
      +    protocol: udp$
$
  Save syslogServers? [y/N, 0 or q]: $
$
$

